{"id": "12th_tamil_u7_q1291", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "12", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_7", "lesson_id": "thonmam_grammar", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "literary_purpose", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "இலக்கியத்தில் ‘தொன்மம்’ (Myth) பயன்படுவதன் முதன்மை நோக்கம் யாது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "பழைய மூடநம்பிக்கைகளைப் பரப்புவது", "B": "இலக்கண விதிகளை விளக்குவது", "C": "மனிதனின் ஆழ்மன உணர்வுகளையும், சமகால வாழ்வியல் உண்மைகளையும் பழங்கதைக் குறியீடுகள் வழி சுருக்கமாகவும் ஆழமாகவும் உணர்த்துவது", "D": "வரலாற்றுக் காலங்களை வரிசைப்படுத்துவது"}, "explanation": "தொன்மம் என்பது பழங்கதைகளை மட்டும் கூறுவதன்று; சமகால மனித உணர்வுகளுக்கும் சமூகப் போராட்டங்களுக்கும் குறியீடாக நின்று ஆழ்ந்த பொருளைத் தரும் உத்தியாகும்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "What is the primary literary function of using a 'Myth' (Thonmam) in poetry and creative writing?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Propagating obsolete superstitions", "B": "Explicating grammatical formulas", "C": "Expressing profound subconscious emotions and contemporary social realities succinctly through ancient archetypal symbols", "D": "Chronologically arranging historical eras"}, "explanation": "Myth functions as an artistic vehicle conveying psychological truths and contemporary relevance through archetypal narratives."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "12", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 185, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "12th Tamil, Unit 7, Page 185", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["Class 12", "Unit 7", "Grammar", "Literary Function"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-05T12:00:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T12:00:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "12th_tamil_u7_q1292", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "easy", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "12", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_7", "lesson_id": "thonmam_grammar", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "saaba_vimosanam", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "புதுமைப்பித்தன் அகலிகையின் தொன்மத்தை மறுவாசிப்பு செய்து படைத்த உலகப்புகழ்பெற்ற சிறுகதை எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கடவுளும் கந்தசாமிப் பிள்ளையும்", "B": "கயிற்றரவு", "C": "செல்லம்மாள்", "D": "சாப விமோசனம்"}, "explanation": "கௌதமரின் சாபத்தால் கல்லான அகலிகை இராமன் பாதம் பட்டுப் பெண்ணானதும், பின் சீதையின் அக்னிப் பிரவேசத்தைக் கேட்டு மீண்டும் கல்லாக விரும்புவதாகப் புதுமைப்பித்தன் 'சாப விமோசனம்' கதையில் படைத்துள்ளார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which celebrated short story did Pudhumaipithan write offering a profound modernist reinterpretation of the Agaligai myth?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Kadavulum Kandhasami Pillaiyum", "B": "Kayitraravu", "C": "Chellammal", "D": "Saaba Vimosanam"}, "explanation": "In 'Saaba Vimosanam', Pudhumaipithan brilliantly reinterprets the myth where Agaligai chooses to turn back into stone upon hearing Sita's ordeal."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "12", "term"